          "title": "You'll want to know: وسيلة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وسيلة — wasīla — \"a means\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "الحافلة وسيلة رخيصة للسفر. al-ḥāfila wasīla rakhīṣa li-s-safar. The bus is a cheap means of travel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وسيلة (wasīla) is built on the native Arabic root w-s-l, \"to seek to draw near\" (Lane). A wasīla is what brings you near to a goal: a means."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
